                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "48a9252a-fa9f-328d-9770-17fc8666baf4",
                        "entry_id": "6a09d3e1-c732-3027-b486-d4572bc20e92",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The action of continuing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "559f9449-e367-4c2b-9cc7-09a6fc655739",
                                "sense_id": "48a9252a-fa9f-328d-9770-17fc8666baf4",
                                "text": "Now stands the Brere like a lord alone, / Puffed up with pryde and vaine pleasaunce. / But all this glee had no continuaunce: / For eftsones winter gan to approche; / The blustering Boreas did encroche, / And beate upon the solitarie Brere; / For nowe no succoure was seene him nere."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "acc45408-17a2-455e-ab51-3214bc7c7758",
                                "sense_id": "48a9252a-fa9f-328d-9770-17fc8666baf4",
                                "text": "In the living state, the body is observed to […] adopt most effectual measures for the permanent continuance of its species."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d1bc0eb-7df4-4e4a-89f4-717ccaaf3b0c",
                                "sense_id": "48a9252a-fa9f-328d-9770-17fc8666baf4",
                                "text": "[…] the interview's continuance already had attracted observation from some topmen aloft and other sailors in the waist or further forward."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c36b8f7a-43c0-4e62-a54d-0e666b15724a",
                                "sense_id": "48a9252a-fa9f-328d-9770-17fc8666baf4",
                                "text": "Universal Directory of Railway Officials and Railway Year Book, 1946-47. […] Although the preparation of the fifty-second edition of this well-known work proved a far from easy task, owing to the continuance of unsettled conditions in many parts of the world, the response to the endeavours of the publishers to obtain accurate and complete information has exceeded anything that would have been possible twelve months earlier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2868376f-390a-425c-a7e4-9304c47aa602",
                                "sense_id": "48a9252a-fa9f-328d-9770-17fc8666baf4",
                                "text": "There is little to report of changes on the Great Eastern Line other than deceleration, doubtless explained by continuance of the electrification work."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "07796797-d1ec-3932-b32b-1d8c338dc8fd",
                        "entry_id": "6a09d3e1-c732-3027-b486-d4572bc20e92",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The period during which something continues or goes on; duration."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2dc7f894-15d5-4fe3-8099-b5882dbdfa5c",
                                "sense_id": "07796797-d1ec-3932-b32b-1d8c338dc8fd",
                                "text": "The gentlemen of the mission were present at a splendid festival, called \"The Yam Custom.\" […] During the continuance of it, (as in the ancient Saturnalia) neither theft, intrigue, nor assault, are punishable, but licentiousness of every kind prevails."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4ad0a5ce-f38f-3c64-a421-b688bb020dc8",
                        "entry_id": "6a09d3e1-c732-3027-b486-d4572bc20e92",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An order issued by a court granting a postponement of a legal proceeding for a set period."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f937f332-dfb8-46b3-b23d-cad72d6de919",
                                "sense_id": "4ad0a5ce-f38f-3c64-a421-b688bb020dc8",
                                "text": "At the submission to sufficient facts in Lowell District Court, an agreement was reached between the prosecution and the defense. Despite the continuance without a finding, the defendant was required to pay court costs of $150. The continuance means that if the defendant is not arrested on the same charge within the next six months, the charge against him will be dropped."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "023c231a-d338-4d77-8b21-c2ca80c6881d",
                                "sense_id": "4ad0a5ce-f38f-3c64-a421-b688bb020dc8",
                                "text": "Where the Department of Homeland Security seeks to re-serve a respondent to effect proper service of a notice to appear that was defective under the regulatory requirements for serving minors under the age of 14, a continuance should be granted for that purpose."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7869506c-54ca-4faa-8f28-64a925e63298",
                        "source_entry_id": "6a09d3e1-c732-3027-b486-d4572bc20e92",
                        "source_sense_description": "The action of continuing",
                        "target_lang_word": "continuation",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "continuation",
